2026-10-16,,Application Developer for the Open MRI Reconstruction Framework (f/m/d),Siemens Healthineers,"Erlangen, Bavaria, Germany",Erlangen,north,Erlangen-Bruck,2.44,1.86,S1,li,"Job Requirements

Do you want to help create the future of healthcare? Our name, Siemens Healthineers, was selected to honor our people who dedicate their energy and passion to this cause. It reflects their pioneering spirit combined with our long history of engineering in the ever-evolving healthcare industry.

We offer you a flexible and dynamic environment with opportunities to go beyond your comfort zone in order to grow personally and professionally. Sounds interesting?

Then come and join our global team as Application Developer (f/m/d) for the Open MRI Reconstruction Framework to deliver tailored solutions to meet the diverse needs of our customers.

Choose the best place for your work – Within the scope of this position, it is possible, in consultation with your manager, to work mobile (within Germany) up to an average volume of 60% of the respective working hours.

Even more flexibility? Mobile working from abroad is possible for up to 30 days a year under certain conditions and in selected countries.

Job location: Allee am Röthelheimpark 2, 91052 Erlangen.

Your Tasks And Responsibilities

You develop and maintain reference implementations, core application building blocks, and tools within the Open Reconstruction application framework, ensuring that MRI researchers can efficiently create and evaluate their own reconstruction applications.

You apply your expertise in MRI physics, image reconstruction, and clinical research workflows to drive the continuous improvement of the Open Recon framework in terms of usability, flexibility, and completeness.

You collaborate closely with research partners and application developers to identify the needs of the MRI research community and turn them into practical framework features, APIs, tools, and workflows.

By developing representative end-to-end use cases and analyzing new application scenarios, you validate the frameworks capabilities, identify gaps, and provide actionable feedback that drives the evolution of the framework.

As part of an agile team, you take ownership of application-level development activities including design, implementation, testing, evaluation, documentation, and knowledge sharing to ensure a productive and seamless developer experience.

To find out more about the specific business, have a look at Magnetic Resonance Imaging.

Your Qualifications And Experience

You hold a Master's degree in medical engineering, physics, computer science, biomedical engineering, or a related field.

You possess several years of professional experience in MRI physics, image reconstruction techniques, and clinical research workflows, enabling you to understand complex research applications and follow discussions on the underlying algorithms.

Alternatively, you hold a PhD in one of these fields.

You possess solid expertise in developing MRI reconstruction applications for clinical and research use cases in C++ and/or Python. Furthermore, you are able to translate these experiences into high-quality application-level software components, tools, and reference implementations.

You have extensive experience working in multidisciplinary clinical and research environments, collaborating closely with radiologists, physicists, researchers, and application specialists, giving you a deep understanding of MRI research workflows, clinical processes, and the practical challenges of translating innovative ideas into daily practice.

Ideally, you have experience with existing MRI research frameworks and image processing pipelines.

Knowledge of machine learning for medical imaging or software development for regulated medical devices and healthcare applications is considered an additional advantage.

﻿Your Attributes And Skills

You have excellent English communication skills, enabling effective collaboration within the team and with international colleagues. Additional knowledge in German is considered a plus.

You have strong teamwork and collaboration skills, including active listening and respectful dialogue.

We win together - that’s why you are dedicated to delivering the best possible solutions to our customers in the area under your responsibility.

You love sharing your insights and experiences, inspiring others to grow alongside you. 

You embrace continuous learning, always exploring new technologies, new application scenarios and sharpening your skills. 

You take pride in crafting software that meets the highest standards of quality and reliability.

Our Global Team

Siemens Healthineers is a leading global medical technology company. 74,000 dedicated colleagues in over 70 countries are driven to shape the future of healthcare. An estimated 5 million patients across the globe benefit every day from our innovative technologies and services in the areas of diagnostic and therapeutic imaging, laboratory diagnostics and molecular medicine, as well as digital health and enterprise services.

Our Culture

Our culture embraces different perspectives, open debate, and the will to challenge convention. Change is a constant aspect of our work. We aspire to lead the change in our industry rather than just react to it. That’s why we invite you to take on new challenges, test your ideas, and celebrate success.

Check our Careers Site at https://careers.siemens-healthineers.com/global/en

As an equal opportunity employer, we welcome applications from individuals with disabilities.

We care about your data privacy and take compliance with GDPR as well as other data protection legislation seriously. For this reason, we ask you not to send us your CV or resume by email. We ask instead that you create a profile in our talent community where you can upload your CV. Setting up a profile lets us know you are interested in career opportunities with us and makes it easy for us to send you an alert when relevant positions become open. Click here to get started.

To All Recruitment Agencies

Siemens Healthineers' recruitment is internally managed, with external support permitted only when a qualified supplier has established a formal contract with us. Unsolicited candidate submissions and referrals, absent a current supplier contract, do not establish consent and are ineligible for fees. We delete and destroy unsolicited information, thus, would recommend you refrain from any such practices. Your adherence to our policies is appreciated.

