 Together we make a difference 

We are a leading provider of innovative, high-performance airport logistics solutions. Our portfolio includes baggage and cargo handling products and solutions, logistics process digitisation software, and a comprehensive range of maintenance and service offerings. Our major clients include well-known airports and airlines worldwide.

We are looking for a working student (m/f/d) product management to join our team in the Baggage Vision area, starting immediately, for 20 hours per week.

Your Responsibilities

Within our Airport Systems division, we build highly automated logistics systems for air cargo terminals at international airports worldwide, as well as software for baggage handling and container terminals. We are seeking a working student (m/f/d) to support product management activities for the Vision & Classification portfolio, which includes 5 products (Baggage Vision, Vision Encoding, Bag Check, Vision AI, and VarioTip vision system).

You will assist the Vision & Classification Product Manager in collecting and developing product-related communication and support materials, and ensuring their structured documentation and accessibility through SharePoint and Vikipedia (our internal encyclopedia). This includes configuration management documentation, collection and analysis of test center unit information, collection of market and competitor research, and the creation of sales presentations to support customer-facing teams.

Qualifications

Strong organizational and documentation skills, with the ability to structure and maintain product information.

Proficiency in Microsoft Office, particularly PowerPoint and Excel, for creating presentations and analyzing data.

Experience with SharePoint, wiki platforms, or knowledge management systems.

Ability to collect, analyze, and summarize technical, product, and market data.

Strong research skills, and ability to translate technical concepts into clear customer-facing and sales support materials.

Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.

Technical curiosity and interest in machine vision, AI, automation, and airport logistics systems.

Self-motivated, detail-oriented, and able to work independently in a cross-functional environment.

What We Offer

The opportunity to work remotely and enjoy flexible working hours to optimally balance your studies and work

A motivated team that supports your professional development

A dynamic, international working environment

Modern offices and a constructive, collaborative team atmosphere

Free on-site parking

How To Contact Us

If you would like to discuss any initial questions directly with our Human Resources department, please contact Sandra Gayduschek at +49 (9131) 17-37536.

We are committed to equal opportunity and welcome applications from people with disabilities.

