Curiosity and hands-on interest in modern packaging and assembly technologies, semiconductor packaging, precision manufacturing, and the construction of advanced electro-optical modules.

Ability to work independently, self-organize, and take ownership of tasks.

Flexibility to adapt to a challenging and dynamic work environment.

Interest in collaborating with international partners and stakeholders.

Good command of spoken and written English, with effective communication skills.

Hands-on experience in electronics development, testing, laboratory work, or telecommunications hardware is preferred.

It would be nice if you also had:

Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.

A proactive and results-oriented approach to work.

Knowledge in digital and analog electrical design techniques

German Proficiency

