ment (30%): Drive continuous improvement initiatives, system upgrades, and the implementation of support packages (LHPs/patches) for SAP HCM. * Oversee the technical architecture and integration of SAP HCM with adjacent HR systems and external interfaces. **What You Bring** * University degree in Information Technology, Business Administration, Human Resources, or a related field. * Longstanding professional experience in SAP HCM consulting, service management, or payroll operations with a strong focus on German Payroll (PY) and Time Management (PT). * Certifications: SAP Certified Application Associate - Human Capital Management; ITIL Foundation Certification * SAP HCM Expertise & Payroll Management: Proficient in SAP HCM Payroll (PY) configuration, troubleshooting, and Time Management (PT) schema customization, along with support package implementation and payroll run monitoring. * Payroll & Compliance Knowledge: In-depth understanding of German labor law, tax, and social security regulations, including audit compliance and payroll reporting standards (DEÜV, ELStAM), as well as data privacy and GDPR compliance in HR systems. * Service & IT Management: Experienced in IT Service Management (ITSM), SLA monitoring, vendor and external provider management, and requirements engineering and business analysis. **About the Team** Our Global Functions are essential in driving the company's pivotal initiatives and ensuring operational excellence across various groups, business areas, and regions. These roles support our vision to become the most valued energy technology company in the world. As part of our team, you contribute to our vision by shaping the global energy transition, partnering with our internal and external collaborators, and conducting business responsibly and in compliance with legal requirements and regulationsin **Who is Siemens Energy?** At Siemens Energy, we are more than just an energy technology company. With ~100.000 dedicated employees in more than 9