Role Summary

We are seeking an outstanding Account Executive Splunk to further develop and grow the business in the german region! This individual will play a key role in executing on important Midmarket and Enterprise customer which are germanies economic backbone. The mission is clear: Helping this industry champions to produce worldclass goods and services with the help of our unique solution, gain productivity and competiveness to scale and grow fast with the result to drive a significant share of revenue for Splunk.

We are looking for an inspiring person. Someone who demonstrates a clear ability to grow businesses, close sophisticated multi-million-dollar transactions while still understanding the need for constant pipeline generation and sustainable revenue flows. You will have done this before; experience, knowledge and ideas are a must.

What You'll Get To Do

Own your revenue goal end-to-end — prospect net-new and land opportunities, build a quality pipeline, and develop, negotiate, and close deals with C-suite and executive buyers.

Serve as the Account Orchestrator: align Splunk's portfolio with each customer's strategic goals and build account plans that grow annual contract value and recurring revenue.

Orchestrate complex, multi-stakeholder deal cycles — navigate the commercial, legal, and technical requirements and lead consultative negotiations that balance pricing, service levels, and contractual commitments.

Analyze data and create forecasts to set weekly, monthly, and quarterly sales commitments.

Maintain deep expertise across Splunk's portfolio and articulate solutions' long-term value and ROI in the customer's context.

Translate cybersecurity and observability trends, market dynamics, and competitive insight into account strategy and relationship maps.

Tap into the broader Cisco ecosystem — both within the combined organization and across the joint Cisco/Splunk channel — to source opportunities, expand accounts, and win deals together.

Partner with internal cross-functional teams (SEs, Customer Success, Delivery, Rev Ops, Finance, Legal, Procurement) to align to GTM processes and move deals forward.

Must-have Qualifications

Minimum 8 years of relevant software industry experience (IT systems, enterprise, or infrastructure management).

Proven track record in proactive business development and closing net-new opportunities

Accurate forecasting and consistent delivery against commitments across long and complex sales cycles

Skilled at orchestrating cross-functional teams through complex sales cycles

Excellent prioritization; able to run multiple concurrent opportunities to deadline

Outstanding communication, presentation, and negotiation skills

Self-motivated, results-oriented team player who thrives in a high-growth environment

Deep understanding of enterprise IT environments, including cloud infrastructure, cybersecurity, observability, data platforms and digital transformation

Experience in SaaS, cybersecurity, observability or enterprise infrastructure is preferred

Strong operational discipline and proficiency with Salesforce or comparable enterprise CRM platforms

Bachelor’s degree or equivalent professional experience; an advanced degree is a plus

Fluent in German and English, both written and spoken

Willingness to travel

Splunk, a Cisco company, is an equal opportunity employer and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, genetic information, age, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected basis

Why Cisco?

At Cisco, we’re revolutionizing how data and infrastructure connect and protect organizations in the AI era – and beyond. We’ve been innovating fearlessly for 40 years to create solutions that power how humans and technology work together across the physical and digital worlds. These solutions provide customers with unparalleled security, visibility, and insights across the entire digital footprint.

Fueled by the depth and breadth of our technology, we experiment and create meaningful solutions. Add to that our worldwide network of doers and experts, and you’ll see that the opportunities to grow and build are limitless. We work as a team, collaborating with empathy to make really big things happen on a global scale. Because our solutions are everywhere, our impact is everywhere.

We are Cisco, and our power starts with you.

