As the largest institute within the Fraunhofer-Gesellschaft, we have been conducting research for over 30 years in diverse fields such as artificial intelligence, microelectronics, sensor systems, data collection, signal processing and transmission. Talents from various engineering and natural science disciplines will find a wide range of exciting research topics under a single roof. A few highlights that reflect our innovative strength: Neuromorphic computing, 5G/6G mobile communication technologies, generative AI in speech and signal processing, and X-ray imaging for e-mobility. And that’s just the beginning! **Which sustainable solutions will you find with us?**

**You are interested in combining research and practices and would like to develop further in the field of behavioral evaluation in complex environments?**

**Then have a look at our offer!**

**Be part of change**

As part of the **»Advanced Speech Research«** group, you will be involved in performing empirical research on the perception and cognition of audio in an interactive virtual environment. In virtual reality, people can explore the simulated environment in both position and orientation, such that no two users produce the same trajectory. In this position, you will develop and evaluate current behavioral evaluation models to assess how groups of users explore complex audiovisual environments. Your work will then be used to analyze the exploration of participants in an empirical study, recording their movements, in a virtual reality setting while being exposed to different auditory signals. Specifically, your role will entail:

* **Dataset Analysis:** You will apply measures of behavioural analysis measures to datasets of human exploration captured in virtual reality to identify current gaps.
* **Proposing New Methods:** You will contribute to ideas about behavioural analysis capturing temporal and dimensions and entropy-related measures.
* **Empirical Research:** You will design and conduct empirical research to gather new 6-DoF behavioural data.
* **Validation:** You will perform statistical analysis of results against baseline data.
* **Scientific Writing:** You will be given the chance to contribute to publishing the research through scientific journals or conferences, in addition to showcasing your results through online datasets.

**What you contribute**

* You are currently **studying** either a bachelor’s or master’s degree related to virtual reality, behavioural sciences, sensory sciences, or a related field.
* **Enjoying creative and collaborative work** in a multidisciplinary field and are eager to learn about topics such as virtual reality and auditory cognition.
* **Strong command of English** for working in an international environment.

**What we offer**

* **Organize your schedule:** Benefit from flexible working hours that are perfectly compatible with your studies.
* **Become part of a creative team:** Experience an open and friendly working atmosphere in which your ideas are valued.
* **Variety that inspires:** Look forward to divers tasks that inspire and challenge you.
* **Shape the future with us:** Take part in application-oriented research and put your theoretical knowledge to practice.
* **Innovation that inspires:** Exciting and pioneering projects that make a real difference.

We will agree your start date and weekly working hours with you **individually** (as a working student **10 to 15 hours per week** or for an internship at least three months) . You can reduce your hours before exams and increase them during semester breaks. You can set your working days flexibly. After your studies, there are attractive opportunities to join the institute on a full-time or part-time basis. You can flexibly determine the working days of your fixed-term employment contract.

