* You have already gained initial practical experience with Large Language Models, such as working with LLM APIs, prompt engineering, or developing your own LLM-based applications
* You have applied your knowledge successfully in university projects, internships, or personal projects

﻿

**Your attributes and skills:**

* You are eager to apply emerging AI technologies to real-world business use cases
* You are curious about recent developments in Large Language Models and AI Agents and enjoy exploring new frameworks and approaches independently
* You work independently, proactively, and in a structured manner while contributing your own ideas
* You value high-quality results and pay attention to clean, maintainable code, clear documentation, and meaningful comments
* You enjoy collaborating with colleagues from different professional backgrounds and can communicate technical concepts in an understandable way
* You are fluent in English, both written and spoken. German language skills are considered an advantage but are not required

**Our global team:**

Siemens Healthineers is a leading global medical technology company. 74,000 dedicated colleagues in over 70 countries are driven to shape the future of healthcare. An estimated 5 million patients across the globe benefit every day from our innovative technologies and services in the areas of diagnostic and therapeutic imaging, laboratory diagnostics and molecular medicine, as well as digital health and enterprise services.

