Founded in 2021, UTN is an innovative university with a focus on artificial intelligence, interdisciplinary research and modern teaching. With flat hierarchies, digital technologies and an open, inclusive culture, it offers a future-orientated working environment. The sustainable campus in Nuremberg will be the centre of a new city district and home to around 6,000 students. The Nuremberg metropolitan region offers a high quality of life, good transport links and an attractive cost of living.

Instructional Designer (m/f/d)

Do you want to rethink teaching and help shape the future of UTN as part of a dedicated, interdisciplinary team? At the Digital LEAD Lab in the UTN School of Students and Young Researchers (StaRs), you’ll support faculty in course design and guide them in further developing their courses to be competency-based, innovative, and effective. You’ll provide guidance on the design of courses and exams, promote the meaningful use of digital formats and technologies, and contribute your expertise to workshops and professional development programs. At the same time, you’ll play a role in quality assurance and the strategic development of digital teaching—in a practical, collaborative manner with creative freedom.

**Interested?**

Then apply now and become part of a unique journey at the Digital LEAD Lab. Together, we’re building the university of the future—with your talent and dedication.  
The position is a two-year fixed-term contract.

**Responsibilities:**
---------------------

* Providing pedagogical guidance and support to faculty in designing learning experiences aligned with the UTN teaching and learning concept
* Providing pedagogical and technical advice and support to faculty members in integrating innovative digital teaching and learning formats and materials
* Designing and implementing professional development and continuing education programs for faculty
* Supporting the structural development of digital teaching

**Profile:**
------------

**Required:**

* A successfully completed master’s degree in educational sciences, pedagogy, educational technology, media education, instructional design, or a comparable field of study. Alternatively, a master’s degree in another field with extensive relevant professional experience; in this case, upon hiring, the position will be classified as E 12 TV-L.
* Expertise in theories, approaches, and practices related to the design of teaching and learning
* Expertise in the field of digitalization in teaching and learning from a socio-technical-didactic perspective
* Very good command of German or English (at least C1 level); in the second language, sufficient proficiency to communicate confidently in day-to-day work, as well as a willingness to continuously improve these skills
* Excellent communication and facilitation skills, a structured and independent work style, and strong teamwork skills

**Desirable:**

* Relevant professional experience in instructional design in a higher education context, including advising, supporting, and training faculty or comparable target groups, as well as designing and conducting workshops or continuing education programs
* Expertise in or a strong interest in the field of learning, teaching, and assessment using AI and/or the creation of audiovisual teaching and learning media (e.g., experience working in a video studio)
* Experience living abroad or prior experience in an intercultural environment

**Benefits:**
-------------

* Attractive salary according to pay group E13 TV-L (for full-time employment, the gross salary starts at €4,629.74 gross, more details at: https://oeffentlicher-dienst.info/tv-l/allg/) with regular pay rises and an increasing salary in line with the collective agreement. If the required academic degree in the above-mentioned subjects is not held, the position will be classified in pay group E12 of the TV-L (starting at €4,310.90 gross) upon hiring.
