2026-10-02,,Product Engineer (m/f/d),Leggett Dynamics,"Nuremberg, Bavaria, Germany",Nürnberg,south,Nürnberg Hbf,1.03,16.7,S1/RE,li,"We, at Leggett Dynamics, are searching for a Product Engineer(m/f/d) within our Engineering team to help support our Automotive business. Did you know we are the world’s leading designer and manufacturer of seating support and comfort systems for transportation manufacturers, as well as tier one and two suppliers within the automotive industry? That’s right! Our automotive products fall into four primary groups: Seating and Lumbar support, Wireless Charging, Motors and Actuators, and Mechanical Cables. If you join our team, your work will ensure people across the world have a little more comfort in their lives.

As a Product Engineer(m/f/d) you will play a key role in developing the next generation of motor solutions and bringing new concepts into series production. Your work will directly influence product performance, quality, cost, and manufacturability while helping us meet customer requirements in a competitive market. You will be part of a collaborative engineering team, working across disciplines to solve technical challenges and deliver robust, high-quality products.

Additionally, You'll

Design and development of DC motors (brushed and brushless) and geared motors, including optimization with respect to performance, efficiency, cost, package space, and acoustics

Perform electromagnetic, thermal, and mechanical calculations and oversee simulation activities

Create technical documentation, CAD models, and engineering drawings

Develop new products and optimize existing products with regard to performance, NVH (Noise, Vibration, and Harshness), and manufacturability

Build, support, and validate prototypes, as well as analyze test data and support production launch activities and continuous product improvements

Analyze test data and support series production launches and product improvements

Coordinate technical topics with customers, suppliers, and development partners

Provide technical guidance and support to design engineers, electronics engineers, and the test engineering department

Manage and coordinate technical activities within international development projects

To Be Successful In This Role, You'll Need

Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electrical Engineering, Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, or a comparable qualification

Minimum of 5 years of professional experience in motor or actuator development, ideally within the automotive industry

Strong expertise in motor design and calculations, simulation, and drive technology, as well as materials engineering and manufacturing technologies

Experience with CAD systems, preferably CATIA V5

Knowledge of materials engineering and manufacturing technologies

Structured, analytical, and solution-oriented approach to work

Excellent communication and collaboration skills in international teams

Good German and English language skills

Automotive industry experience is preferred

What To Do Next

Now that you’ve had a chance to learn more about us, what are you waiting for! Apply today and allow us the opportunity to learn more about you and the value you can bring to our team. Once you apply, be sure to create a profile, and sign up for job alerts, so you can be the first to know when new opportunities become available. If you require assistance completing an application, please contact our team at careers@leggett.com

Our Values

Our values speak to our shared beliefs, and describe how we approach working together.

Put People First reflects our commitment to safety and care of each other, learning and development, and creating an inclusive environment of mutual respect, empathy and belonging.

Do the Right Thing focuses us on acting with honesty and integrity, delivering the results the right way, taking pride in our work, and speaking the truth – good or bad.

Do Great Work…Together occurs when we engage without hierarchy, collaborate as a team, embrace challenges, and work for the good of all of us.

Take Ownership and Raise the Bar demonstrates our responsibility to add value and make a difference, challenge the status quo and biases to make things better, foster innovative and creative solutions to drive impact, and explore new perspectives and embrace change.

Our Commitment to You

We're actively taking steps to make sure our culture is inclusive and that our processes and practices promote equity for all. Leggett & Platt is comprised of people of all abilities, gender identities and expressions, ages, ethnicities, sexual orientations, veteran status, and more. Join us!

Germany Benefits Include

Free coffee, free water

Phone and laptop

Flexible working hours

Mobile work

Possibility to work part-time

Company events (e.g. Christmas party, summer party)

Private pension supplement

30 days vacation, option for additional unpaid leave

Chance to contribute your own ideas

We welcome and encourage applications if you meet the minimum qualifications. Even if you do not meet the preferred qualifications, we’d love the opportunity to consider you.

