Do you want to help create the future of healthcare? Our name, Siemens Healthineers, was selected to honor our people who dedicate their energy and passion to this cause. It reflects their pioneering spirit combined with our long history of engineering in the ever-evolving healthcare industry.

We offer you a flexible and dynamic environment with opportunities to go beyond your comfort zone in order to grow personally and professionally. Sounds interesting?

**Your Role:**

Are you passionate about medical technology, healthcare innovation, and the future of healthcare? Do you want to combine your scientific or technical background with business expertise?

Then the part-time MBA program with practical assignments in Sales, Marketing and Business Development is the perfect opportunity for you.

The program provides advanced knowledge and skills in business leadership, value chain optimization, as well as analytical and management methods, all within an international and sustainability-focused context.

Starting on September 1, 2027, you will combine your Master's studies at Friedrich-Alexander University Erlangen-Nuremberg with an exciting practical role in Sales, Marketing and Business Development at Siemens Healthineers in Forchheim.

You will support our team in projects related to market development, customer and competitive analyses, marketing campaigns, business development initiatives, and sales performance management. You will analyze market and business data, identify growth opportunities, and derive recommendations for action that support our international sales and marketing organizations.

Modern digital technologies, data analytics, and AI applications will help you identify market trends, better understand customer needs, and develop data-driven recommendations for management decision-making. Working closely with international sales teams, marketing experts and business leaders, you will actively contribute to shaping the future of healthcare.

You are enthusiastic about digitalization, IT, and artificial intelligence, and you enjoy exploring new technologies and helping drive their adoption. With your analytical mindset, curiosity, and initiative, you will contribute your own ideas and help develop innovative approaches to advancing our global business.

Look forward to diverse responsibilities in an international environment, valuable insights into the commercial side of a global healthcare leader, and the opportunity to help bring meaningful innovations to market.

**What you can expect:**

* Program start: September 1, 2027
* Program duration: 18 months
* Master's studies at Friedrich-Alexander University in Nuremberg
* Practical assignments within our departments in Forchheim and potentially abroad
* During the first and second semesters, block courses in Acting, Leading & Analyzing; lectures take place in Nuremberg on Friday afternoons and Saturdays
* During the third semester, you will focus on your Master's thesis

**What you bring:**

* Bachelor's degree in Medical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Life Sciences, Biomedicine, Industrial Engineering with a focus on Healthcare or a comparable field of study
* At least one year of practical experience (e.g., internships or working student positions)
* Strong interest in Sales, Marketing and Business Development, ideally demonstrated through initial practical experience in commercial, marketing, business development, customer-facing, or project-based roles, as well as international or intercultural experience
* Strong affinity for data analytics, digitalization, and artificial intelligence, including initial experience with AI-based tools
* Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and PowerPoint
* Excellent written and spoken German (C1) and English skills; additional language skills are considered an advantage
* Structured and independent working style, quick comprehension, reliability, and a strong willingness to learn
* Passion for healthcare and medical innovation

**What we offer you:**

* Monthly salary of €2,310.00
* Full coverage of tuition fees amounting to approximately €25,000
* Flexible working hours, opportunities to work from home, and of course the necessary technical equipment
* 35-hour work week (Monday to Friday), including paid time off for lectures and exams
* 30 vacation days per calendar year
* Excellent career and employment opportunities upon successful completion of your studies

**What is important to us:**

* We value diverse perspectives because they broaden our horizons.
* We believe in open communication because it helps us move forward together.
* We are open to new ways of doing things and embrace change proactively.
* We foster an inclusive environment where everyone can be themselves.
* We provide equal opportunities for all applicants, regardless of disability, background, or culture.

We look forward to receiving your application!

**Our global team:**

Siemens Healthineers is a leading global medical technology company. 74,000 dedicated colleagues in over 70 countries are driven to shape the future of healthcare. An estimated 5 million patients across the globe benefit every day from our innovative technologies and services in the areas of diagnostic and therapeutic imaging, laboratory diagnostics and molecular medicine, as well as digital health and enterprise services.

**Our culture:**

Our culture embraces different perspectives, open debate, and the will to challenge convention. Change is a constant aspect of our work. We aspire to lead the change in our industry rather than just react to it. That’s why we invite you to take on new challenges, test your ideas, and celebrate success.

Check our Careers Site at https://careers.siemens-healthineers.com/global/en

As an equal opportunity employer, we welcome applications from individuals with disabilities.

Wish to find out more before applying? Contact us: ausbildung@siemens-healthineers.com, if you wish to discuss any initial questions with our recruitment team.

We care about your data privacy and take compliance with GDPR as well as other data protection legislation seriously. For this reason, we ask you not to send us your CV or resume by email. We ask instead that you create a profile in our talent community where you can upload your CV. Setting up a profile lets us know you are interested in career opportunities with us and makes it easy for us to send you an alert when relevant positions become open. Click here to get started.

