Based in Germany 

Focus: PHP · Java · High-Resilience Platforms · AI-Enhanced Engineering

The role: 

We’re on the lookout for an inquisitive, sharp-minded Backend Developer to join our team and help shape the robust, mission-critical infrastructure that powers FinTech and payment operations.

This isn’t about checking off buzzwords on a resume. We need someone who can dissect complexity, reason through challenges, and engineer dependable solutions, because in our world, speed, stability, and precision are everything.

What You’ll Be Working With

You’ll develop and maintain the transaction-processing systems that form the backbone of financial services — where reliability is never optional. Our engineering culture is built on teamwork, modern practices, and continuous improvement:

Agile workflows and iterative development

Collaborative code reviews and open technical discussion

Rigorous, automated testing strategies

Large-scale backend architectures and transaction engines

Uncompromising standards for clean, maintainable code

Daily integration of Claude and other AI development tools

AI is deeply embedded in our process — and it’s here to stay. That means we need developers who don’t just accept AI-generated code at face value: you’ll understand, question, debug, and elevate what it produces.

Who We Hope to Find

While PHP is our primary language, we’re equally interested in strong backend engineers coming from Java or other solid technical backgrounds. We care far more about how you think than exactly what you’ve listed.

Your background could be:

Formal software engineering or computer science training

Mathematics, physics, or another analytical field

Building production systems in PHP, Java, or Python

AI, machine learning, or research and development

Agency work, consultancy, or freelance projects

Self-directed learning or an unconventional career journey

Our team has grown from all kinds of professional paths — the common thread is sharp analysis, genuine curiosity, and real enthusiasm for FinTech and payment technology.

What Matters Most to Us

Clear, logical problem-solving and analytical depth

A rock-solid grasp of software engineering principles

Confidence working within — and improving — large, intricate systems

Keen interest in building fast, always-available applications

Ability to use AI development tools responsibly and critically

Respect for quality: testing, reviews, and code that stands the test of time

A proactive approach to learning and growing your skills

Excitement about financial technology, banking, or payment infrastructure

Direct experience in banking or payments is a bonus — but your mindset and drive count for more.

