This senior leadership role owns the global Circularity Services line within Electrification & Automation Customer Service, covering spare parts, MV/LV retrofits, lifecycle extensions and digitally enabled product services. The role extends the useful life of customers’ installed assets while increasing availability, speed, quality and sustainable business value.

The role carries end-to-end accountability for the strategic and commercial performance of the service line. Reporting to the Electrification & Automation Customer Service Head, the Head leads through a global matrix, develops regional Customer Service leaders, and scales product-related services through standardization, automation and effective execution.

**How You'll Make an Impact**

**Strategic Vision & Ownership**

* Own the global Circularity Services business, defining strategy, targets and portfolio direction across spare parts, MV/LV retrofits, lifecycle extensions and digitally enabled product services.
* Develop scalable offerings that extend asset lifecycles, improve availability and strengthen customer retention and sustainable growth.
* Translate customer, market and installed-base needs into portfolio roadmaps, commercial opportunities and differentiated OEM service value.

**Business & Financial Leadership**

* Hold end-to-end P&L accountability for revenue, profitability, cash, productivity, pricing, investments and overall portfolio performance.
* Drive profitable growth by scaling retrofit, spare-parts, lifecycle-extension and e-business models across countries and customer segments.
* Increase margins and scalability through automation, standardization and streamlined order-to-delivery processes while managing commercial and delivery risks.

**Global Leadership & Collaboration**

* Lead through influence across a global matrix, aligning regions, Business Units, Operations and functional partners behind common priorities.
* Develop, coach and mentor Customer Service leaders across regions, strengthening leadership capability and organizational maturity.
* Mobilize cross-functional and partner capabilities and act as a trusted partner to the Service Head and Business Unit Leadership.

**Operational Excellence & Governance**

* Establish scalable operating models for spare parts, retrofits, lifecycle extensions and digitally enabled product-service delivery.
* Improve availability, lead-time reliability, first-time-right execution, quality and customer transparency through process excellence and automation.
* Drive performance governance and ensure compliance with environmental health and safety, cybersecurity, data protection, export control, ethical and regulatory requirements.

**Customer & Market Focus**

* Improve customer outcomes through greater asset availability, delivery reliability, service quality and measurable lifecycle value.
* Enable countries and channels with standardized offerings, pricing frameworks, commercial plays and required delivery capabilities.
* Use customer, market and installed-base insights to identify growth opportunities and shape future circularity and product-service offerings.

**What You Bring**

* Extensive senior leadership experience in product-related services, operations, business development or portfolio leadership within a technology-driven industry.
* Proven record of driving profitable growth with significant P&L responsibility in spare parts, retrofits, lifecycle extensions, e-business or comparable scalable service models.
* Demonstrated ability to improve productivity and scalability through automation, process transformation and standardized operating models.
* Strong experience leading through influence in international matrix organizations and developing leaders across regions.
* Relevant technical understanding of electrification, automation, industrial products, lifecycle services or comparable fields, combined with strong learning agility.
* Executive-level communication, customer orientation and sound judgment in portfolio, pricing, investment and commercial decisions.

**What We Offer**

* Attractive share programs, allowing you to become a Siemens shareholder and participate directly in the company's long-term success.
* A global organization of outstanding engineers and an executive environment that treats technology as a strategic asset.
* Comprehensive health management, including regular executive health check-ups and programs to support your physical and mental wellbeing.
* Access to global development programs that can be tailored to your individual aspirations and ambitions.
* Accessible locations, international childcare options, and an inspiring work environment where you can bring your whole personality to the table.

